\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Opens Steady Amid Mixed  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Signals \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 08:21\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened stable Friday and the mixed signals from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's refinancing auction late Thursday will hold the leu at current levels for now, say traders. \par \par \uc2  "The results of the refinancing auction were too confusing to interpret," said a trader with a foreign bank in Romania. "I think the leu will remain steady." \par \par \uc2  The leu opened Friday at between 6,900 and 7,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered 300 billion lei in its weekly refinancing auction for banks in overdraught Thursday but dem totaled 582 billion. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offer last week was 500 billion lei. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the demand shows a scarcity of lei on the market. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the same time cut refinancing interest rates to 205% yearly on 15-day loans from 220% in last week's auction. \par \par \uc2  This weeks auction showed the same mixed signals as last week's auction when the rate dropped from 226% the previous week and the offer dropped from 600 billion lei. \par \par \uc2  Another trader said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials told him Thursday they were "ready to buy dollars at between 6,900 lei and 6,950 lei." \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will definitely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they see asks at 6,850 lei or below," he said. "This was made very clear to me." \par \par \uc2  Howe he said the leu will likely remain stable Friday without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Several traders say the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBR) has phoned them during the week saying it was ready to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Another trader predicted the leu could strengthen slightly over the\par next week or so as large companies sell dollars to pay taxes in April.\par     --Adam Brown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 28-03-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0721GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt3s00556\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
