\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2 /IMF -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  `Worrisome' \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1996\par 14:45\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The IMF "supported flexible management of the exchange rate, accompanied by tight financial and incomes policies to reduce inflation," the report said. \par \par \uc2  The IMF suspended disbursement of loan tranches in March after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  withdrew dealer authorization from all but four of the country's 22 banks, bringing inter-bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade to a virtual standstill and triggering a 10% slide in the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at exchange bureaus. \par \par \uc2  A series of recent hikes in the price of energy has pushed inflation up to 40%, away from the 20% annual inflation rate target specified in the IMF loan agreement. \par \par \uc2  While the government has admitted the 20% target is unlikely, claiming instead a figure of around 30%, independent analysts are forecasting a figure between 70% and 100%. \par \par \uc2  The report said the IMF regarded renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market and the bank's accomodation of pressures for credit to agriculture as "worrisome reversions to non-market-oriented policies" which had contributed to "a rapid expansion of credit and an unsustainable widening of the balance of payments deficit during 1995." \par \par \uc2  The IMF had encouraged authorities to improve the quality of data on the monetary and national accounts, the report said, as well as those on the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the major state-owned enterprises that had large losses or arrears. \par \par \uc2  In light of Romania's fragile external position, the report said, it was "imperative" to avoid further policy slippages or reversals which could undermine confidence in the economy, jeopardizing economic recovery and posing a risk to the country's external position. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 13-09-96 \par \par \uc2  1245GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 1896 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013ds9d00h3t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
