\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank says building  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fund. \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, March 22 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will amass an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund to allow it to play an active role in its reformed, market-maker-based, local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, National Bank of Romania vice governor Vlad Soare said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be more involved in that market," Soare told Reuters after announcing that the bank will limit interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer licences to four banks. "We will create...an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund. What we buy from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will go back to the market as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the situation where the market requires it," he said. \par \par \uc2  Soare denied that the changes were an attempt to hold the value of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which slid around 65 percent in a year due to current account problems. \par \par \uc2  He said he expected some continued depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in line with inflationary expectations of around 20 percent this year, down from 27 percent last year. \par \par \uc2  "This doesn't mean somebody is trying to stabilise the rate of exchange," Soare said. \par \par \uc2  He said he had warned both the new market makers and the broker banks that while being responsible and disciplined they could not try to peg the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back. \par \par \uc2  "The rate of exchange will be further depreciated in line with what we expect from inflation," he said. "So I told them, the dealers and all the other banks, that they will make a big mistake if they will keep the rate fixed otherwise the bill we all have to pay will be much higher." -- Peter Bale, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds3m0a259\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
