\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Romania - Feb 7. \b0\par\par\uc2 607 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Feb 7 (Reuter) - Here are highlights of stories in Romania's press on Wednesday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy: \par \par \uc2  Business: \par \par \uc2  BURSA \par \par \uc2  - Quality of macro-economic policies depends on cooperation between government and National Bank, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Daniel Daianu says in interview. \par \par \uc2  ROMANIA LIBERA \par \par \uc2  - Fuel oil consumption in thermal power stations averages daily 5,000 tonnes and stocks are quickly running out. \par \par \uc2  ADEVARUL \par \par \uc2  - International Monetary Fund and World Bank have allegedly frozen loan traches for Romania. \par \par \uc2  - Government and National Bank of Romania are working out measures to strengthen finacial and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  discipline, including corporates' obligations to convert hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into lei to pay internal debts. \par \par \uc2  TINERETUL LIBER \par \par \uc2  - Rom Telecom telephone operator held tender to acquire 2.5 million phone cards and will select best bid in three weeks. \par \par \uc2  ZIUA \par \par \uc2  - Statistics show private sector took 45 percent of Romania's 1995 gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  - Bucharest stock exchange had all-time record turnover at Tuesday's session. \par \par \uc2  LIBERTATEA \par \par \uc2  - Prime Minister Nicolae Vacaroiu said privatisation pace was normal. \par \par \uc2  CRONICA ROMANA \par \par \uc2  - President Ion Iliescu asked county prefects to take steps in support of faster subscription for shares in state companies going private under mass selloff. \par \par \uc2  General: \par \par \uc2  ROMANIA LIBERA \par \par \uc2  - Austrian police arrested 16 Romanians allegedly involved in drug traffic and confiscated 70 kg of heroin. \par \par \uc2  - Adrian Nastase, executive president of ruling Party of Social Democracy (PDSR) said PDSR would reject and comment in the toughest possible way the presidential campaign of former Prime Minister Petre Roman. \par \par \uc2  - Parliament's upper Senate adopted law on refugees. \par \par \uc2  - Interview with Viorel Catarama, vice-president of opposition National Liberal Party on "Contract with Romania", opposition Democratic Convention (CDR) bloc's governing programme. \par \par \uc2  - Report on snowfalls and blizzards in Romania. \par \par \uc2  ADEVARUL \par \par \uc2  - Iulian Radulescu, Gypsies' self-styled emperor, said Gypsies would vote for ruling PDSR in local and parliamentary polls and back its candidate for 1996 presidential elections. \par \par \uc2  - As many as 3,000 people filed request for status of refugee in Romania since 1991, showed statistics by Romanian Emigration Committee. \par \par \uc2  - Opposition 1993 Liberal Party (PL 93) will announce its own candidate for presidential elections after local polls due in April, said PL 93 executive president Horia Rusu. \par \par \uc2  - Romanian government will grant 1.2 billion lei ($444,000) in aid to people affected by earthquacke in China. \par \par \uc2  EVENIMENTUL ZILEI \par \par \uc2  - Excerpts from shorthand report on National Salvation Front council's meeting on December 27, 1989 saying France and the U.S. had agreed to military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by former Soviet Union in \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - Next week ruling PDSR and Romanian National Unity Party (PUNR) to negotiate communcations portfolio left vacant after dismissal of (PUNR) minister Adrian Turicu last week. \par \par \uc2  - PDSR asks managers of research institutes to join party, union leader Radu Minea said. \par \par \uc2  ZIUA \par \par \uc2  - Romania's first test-tube baby was born in clinic in western city of Timisoara. \par \par \uc2  - Report on alleged Russian and Ukrainian mafia gangs active in ex-communist East European countries. \par \par \uc2  - Romania's main difficulties in integration with European Union (EU) are economic and legislative, said EU MP Catherine Lalumiere. \par \par \uc2  LIBERTATEA \par \par \uc2  - Snowfalls and feezing temperatures will continue, weather forecasters warn. \par \par \uc2  CURIERUL NATIONAL \par \par \uc2  - Radu Campeanu, former presidential candidate in first post-communist elections in 1990 and leader of National Liberal Party, will run again for presidency in 1996 elections. \par \par \uc2  - At least 100 from some 3,000 newborn babies in Bucharest's main maternity clinic are abandoned every year, said doctor Ana Culcer. \par \par \uc2  COTIDIANUL \par \par \uc2  - Presidential adviser Paul Dobrescu told journalists that only state media reporters would travel from now on with President Ion Iliescu on his domestic visits. -- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2701tqb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
