\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania central bank \highlight\uc2  confirms  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Dec 20 (Reuter) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the inter-bank market, selling and buying dollars on Tuesday and said it stood ready to do so again if necessary to smooth the local leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We bought dollars to make banks adjust their exposure and observe rules, we sold to smooth out the market but overall the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was net buyer," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager Adrian Grigoriu told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday dealers reported the BNR was active in its support for the leu, which firmed some 10 units to 2,790 to the dollar at close. \par \par \uc2  "The leu trades now between 2,720 and 2,790 against the dollar on the inter-bank market," Grigoriu said, adding that the BNR was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again "to assure good functioning of the inter-bank market." \par \par \uc2  However on the banks' dealing screens the leu was quoted in a wide range from a strong rate of 2,565/50 at a local state bank to 2,695/95 at the ING Bucharest branch. \par \par \uc2  The leu, under pressure over the past three months when it fell by around 30 percent, has gained some ground after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightened monetary policy, increasing key rates and limiting overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure. \par \par \uc2  Last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the discount rate to 35 percent from 30 percent and overdrafts to 110 from 100 percent. It also said it bought more than $20 million at penal exchange rates to enforce discipline on the inter-bank market. -- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drck00lj3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
