\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian leu closes firm on 2,800, money market up. \b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Dec 13 (Reuter) - The Romanian leu closed more or less unchanged and firm at 2,800 to the dollar, with dealers saying the drought of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed ready to break. \par \par \uc2  "I think the volume is starting to come back," said a trader at one of the big four state-owned banks which have worked with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reinforce the fragile leu. \par \par \uc2  The state bank trader said customer and inter-bank volume rose sharply on Wednesday to between $15 million and $18 million, up from perhaps $10.0 million a day in recent days. \par \par \uc2  "I think they were expecting it to go weaker but the rates are stabilising so they started to sell. There is still a lack of liquidity but it is starting to move," he said. \par \par \uc2  Romanian dealers have complained for weeks about a chronic lack of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Though dollar hoarding is usual with the approach of winter it has been greater than normal, helping drive the leu sharply lower over the past two months. \par \par \uc2  Even private commercial banks, cynical about the dual role played out between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the state-owned banks in supporting the leu, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed somewhat firmer. \par \par \uc2  While the state banks continued to quote the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 2,549/30 the commercial banks displayed significantly weaker rates. ING Bucharest, for example, was on 2,750/50. \par \par \uc2  "I'd say the close today is really 2,800-2,820," said a trader at one private commercial bank. "I think it will go step by step and will be firmer as the week goes by." \par \par \uc2  Commercial dealers said activity was minimal. \par \par \uc2  The big four state-owned banks acknowledge they have been working more or less in concert with the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drops below 2,600. \par \par \uc2  So far the interevention has been limited to phone calls to remind dealers where their real interests lie. \par \par \uc2  The message has yet to get to the retail exchange shops which, despite government warnings they will be shut down, prefer to sell the leu at 3,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  That and the 2,800 level on the inter-bank market makes the National Bank's reference rate, computed as a weighted average based on reports from traders, of 2,554 look a little out of kilter with the activity of the real market. \par \par \uc2  State bank dealers, however, said there was greater purchasing volume available at around 2,600 than the 2,800 offered by some of the commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were pleased to see rises in money market rates a week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised refinancing rates 5.0 points to 65 percent. One-week money rose to 54.89 percent from 54.69 and 12-month rates to 52.69 percent from 52.39. \par \par \uc2  Romanian interbank money market rates are on  RBOR. The interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is on  FOREXROM. \par \par \uc2  -- Peter Bale, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drcd00tum\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
