\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Romania - Feb 21. \b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Feb 21 (Reuter) - Here are highlights of stories in Romania's press on Tuesday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy: \par \par \uc2  Business: \par \par \uc2  Evenimentul Zilei - Strikes across Romania -- real reason for strike at engineering plant in Resita is low standard of living; port workers in Constanta and Braila went on strike; workers at IAR planemaker in Brasov stop work on Tuesday (p 3). \par \par \uc2  Romania Libera - Banca Comerciala Romana cuts lending rates by eight percentage points (p 5). \par \par \uc2  - State Ownership Fund approved credit of 15 billion lei ($8.3 million) to Dacia carmaker for manufacture of new car model this year (p 9). \par \par \uc2  Adevarul - Finance Ministry denies rumours that petrol price will go up (p 1). \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources say leu's exchange rate is not set artificially but it is result of demand and offer on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market (p 5). \par \par \uc2  - Officials discuss payment arrears in economy in newspaper's economic debate section (p 6). \par \par \uc2  Azi - Telephone charges on domestic calls will go up starting March 1 (p 2). \par \par \uc2  - Romania has pledged to restructure its industry under association accord with EU (p 4). \par \par \uc2  Libertatea - Tarom jacks up plane fares for domestic flights (p 1). \par \par \uc2  - Romania's water authority RGAB raised water price to 250 leu per cubic metre from 186 lei starting mid-Feb (p 1). \par \par \uc2  General: \par \par \uc2  Evenimentul Zilei - Editorial says further disputes inside Romania's opposition will lead to leftist victory in next year's elections (p 1). \par \par \uc2  - Excerpts from parliamentary report on December 1989 revolution say "terrorists" come to Sibiu to help dictator Nicolae Ceausescu's son Nicu belonged to army's intelligence department (p 2). \par \par \uc2  - Hungarian Democratic Union (HDUR) plans to break association with Democratic Convention (DC) opposition alliance, says HDUR executive leader Takacs Csaba (p 4). \par \par \uc2  Romania Libera - Protocol signed by three parties with ruling Party of Social Democracy (PSD) prepares ground for pardon of former communist politburo members tried and sentenced for crimes committed in December 1989 allowing them to reenter political arena (p 3). \par \par \uc2  - Socialist Labour Party (SLP) demands law forbidding MPs to leave parties on whose lists they were elected (p 3). \par \par \uc2  - Johannes Hallauer, coordinator of anti-AIDS programme of World Health Organisation, says Romanian health ministry should compensate HIV-positive persons who were infected through blood transfusions (p 9). \par \par \uc2  Curierul National - Over 540 prisoners -- of which 75 committed cruel crimes -- are mentally disturbed (p 1). \par \par \uc2  Azi - Sources close to President Ion Iliescu say he often consults with former politburo members considering their experience in communist times (p 2). \par \par \uc2  - Interview with Sergiu Cunescu, head of Social Democratic Party (RSDP), saying social democracy is solution for Romanian society (p 5). \par \par \uc2  Vocea Romaniei - Moldovan Foreign Minister Mihai Popov says in December 1989 NPP leaders including Corneliu Coposu went to the Russian embassy in Bucharest to thank Gorbachev for not approving a Soviet military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  (p 2). -- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr2l00z3z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\p