ns under Softwin-Clemessy Romanian-French partnership (p 13). \par \par \uc2  Libertatea \par \par \uc2  - Romania tests Euromissile's Milan missiles for possible cooperation with French company (p 1). \par \par \uc2  - Gara de Nord railway station will get new look by 2005 under $70 million upgrading project (p 1). \par \par \uc2  General: \par \par \uc2  Evenimentul Zilei \par \par \uc2  - Romania will send some 900 military to Angola to enter UN peace-keeping forces next month (p 3). \par \par \uc2  - Meeting between President Ion Iliescu and leaders of opposition parties on Romania's integration into EU failed to result in common approach on subject (p 2). \par \par \uc2  Curierul National \par \par \uc2  - In news conference in London, Hungarian Democratic Union (HDUR) leader Bela Marko accused Romanian government of trying to assimilate ethnic Hungarians. He said local self-rule was sole way to stop that (p 1-3). \par \par \uc2  Romania Libera \par \par \uc2  - Education Minister Liviu Maior has been sued for insulting and beating Romanian citizen (p 9). \par \par \uc2  - Court found guilty of slander and fined Timisoara journalist who accused former colonel of terrorising people trying to leave Romania during Nicolae Ceausescu's rule (p 16). \par \par \uc2  Adevarul \par \par \uc2  - Coalminers' leaders urged government to renounce closing mines and asked it to give mining sector 981 billion lei ($ 545.9 million) in subsidies under 1995 budget (p 10). \par \par \uc2  Cronica Romana \par \par \uc2  - Big earthquake is expected to shake Romania around 2004 (p 1). \par \par \uc2  Azi \par \par \uc2  - Civic Alliance Party calls for reorganisation of opposition Democratic Convention (p 3). \par \par \uc2  -- Bucharest Newsroom, 40-1 3120264 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr2a019nm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
