\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian leu edges down, dealers see weakness. \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Jan 26 (Reuter) - Romania's leu edged down to 1,778/90 to the dollar on the interbank market after clinging to 1,775/85 over recent days. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it might end the week a little weaker. \par \par \uc2  "The leu might end the week a whisker weaker if the National Bank does not step in the market," said Cosmin Calinescu, Banca Romana pentru Dezvoltare chief dealer. \par \par \uc2  Calinescu said he had not detected any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week. On Monday, dealers said the BNR sold dollars last week to keep the leu stable at 1,774 to the dollar. The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was a shortage of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market but they declined to make long-term forecasts on the leu's exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "Market players are unwilling to sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current rates and buyers on the other hand are reluctant to bid higher," one of them said. \par \par \uc2  Traders were pessimistic about the state of the local market, saying that trading between banks was almost "dead". \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they believed the BNR has resources to keep the domestic market balanced but they wondered for how long. -- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr1q04ega\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
